 \\times \\mathbf{c}\\), \\(\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a}\\), and \\(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\):\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ -11 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 1 + \\sqrt{5} & 4 & -5 \\end{vmatrix} = \\mathbf{i} (5 \\cdot (-5) - 2 \\cdot 4) - \\mathbf{j} (-11 \\cdot (-5) - 2 \\cdot (1 + \\sqrt{5})) + \\mathbf{k} (-11 \\cdot 4 - 5 \\cdot (1 + \\sqrt{5})) = \\mathbf{i} (-25 - 8) - \\mathbf{j} (55 - 2 - 2\\sqrt{5}) + \\mathbf{k} (-44 - 5 - 5\\sqrt{5}) = \\begin{pmatrix} -33 \\\\ -53 + 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ -49 - 5\\sqrt{5} \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 + \\sqrt{5} & 4 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\end{vmatrix} = \\mathbf{i} (4 \\cdot 0 - (-5) \\cdot 3) - \\mathbf{j} ((1 + \\sqrt{5}) \\cdot 0 - (-5) \\cdot 1) + \\mathbf{k} ((1 + \\sqrt{5}) \\cdot 3 - 4 \\cdot 1) = \\mathbf{i} (15) - \\mathbf{j} (5) + \\mathbf{k} (3 + 3\\sqrt{5} - 4) = \\begin{pmatrix} 15 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1 + 3\\sqrt{5} \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -11 & 5 & 2 \\end{vmatrix} = \\mathbf{i} (3 \\cdot 2 - 0 \\cdot 5) - \\mathbf{j} (1 \\cdot 2 - 0 \\cdot (-11)) + \\mathbf{k} (1 \\cdot 5 - 3 \\cdot (-11)) = \\mathbf{i} (6) - \\mathbf{j} (2) + \\mathbf{k} (5 + 33) = \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 38 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nNow, we compute \\(3 (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}) - 8 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a}) + k (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})\\):\n\\[\n3 (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}) = 3 \\begin{pmatrix} -33 \\\\ -53 + 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ -49 - 5\\sqrt{5} \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -99 \\\\ -159 + 6\\sqrt{5} \\\\ -147 - 15\\sqrt{5} \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\\[\n-8 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a}) = -8 \\begin{pmatrix} 15 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1 + 3\\sqrt{5} \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -120 \\\\ 40 \\\\ 8 - 24\\sqrt{5} \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\\[\nk (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}) = k \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 38 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6k \\\\ -2k \\\\ 38k \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\\[\n3 (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}) - 8 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a}) + k (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}) = \\begin{pmatrix} -99 \\\\ -159 + 6\\sqrt{5} \\\\ -147 - 15\\sqrt{5} \\end{pmatrix} + \\begin{pmatrix} -120 \\\\ 40 \\\\ 8 - 24\\sqrt{5} \\end{pmatrix} + \\begin{pmatrix} 6k \\\\ -2k \\\\ 38k \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -219 + 6k \\\\ -119 + 6\\sqrt{5} - 2k \\\\ -139 - 15\\sqrt{5} + 38k \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nFor the vectors to be orthogonal, their dot product must be zero:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} -9 + \\sqrt{5} \\\\ 12 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{pmatrix} -219 + 6k \\\\ -119 + 6\\sqrt{5} - 2k \\\\ -139 - 15\\sqrt{5} + 38k \\end{pmatrix} = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n(-9 + \\sqrt{5})(-219 + 6k) + 12(-119 + 6\\sqrt{5} - 2k) + (-3)(-139 - 15\\sqrt{5} + 38k) = 0\n\\]\nExpanding each term:\n\\[\n(-9)(-219) + (-9)(6k) + (\\sqrt{5})(-219) + (\\sqrt{5})(6k) + 12(-119) + 12(6\\sqrt{5}) + 12(-2k) + (-3)(-139) + (-3)(-15\\sqrt{5}) + (-3)(38k)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 1971 - 54k - 219\\sqrt{5} + 6k\\sqrt{5} - 1428 + 72\\sqrt{5} - 24k + 417 + 45\\sqrt{5} - 114k\n\\]\nCombining like terms:\n\\[\n= 1971 - 1428 + 417 - 54k - 24k - 114k + (-219 + 72 + 45)\\sqrt{5} + 6k\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\\[\n= 960 - 192k + (-219 + 117)\\sqrt{5} + 6k\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\\[\n= 960 - 192k - 102\\sqrt{5} + 6k\\sqrt{5} = 0\n\\]\nSince the \\(\\sqrt{5}\\) terms must cancel out, we get:\n\\[\n-192k + 6k\\sqrt{5} - 102\\sqrt{"},"grade":{"answer":"[102]","correct":false,"format":"other","parseable":true},"id":"precalculus:19"}
